{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5007e9a5-33ed-403c-a4e1-57142c6777d4",
    "name": "NPHIIS Screening API",
    "description": "Screening intake for NPHIIS (hie-auth `POST /provider/screenings`).\n\nA screening system sends a screened person as plain JSON. The service matches an existing FHIR `Patient` by identifier type + number (or creates one), then stores point of entry, travel history and signs/symptoms as a `QuestionnaireResponse` linked to that patient.\n\n**Auth:** Bearer JWT, like every other NPHIIS API. The screening service has its own user account: run **Auth > Login** to obtain `{{token}}` (and `{{refresh_token}}`), and **Auth > Refresh Token** before it expires. All other requests inherit the collection's Bearer auth.\n\n**Idempotent** on `screeningId`: resubmitting the same id returns `duplicate: true` and creates nothing.\n\n| Status | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| 201 / 200 | Created a patient / matched an existing one |\n| 400 | Invalid payload; `errors[]` lists every problem |\n| 401 | Missing, invalid or expired token |\n| 409 | Identifiers match more than one patient (`patientIds[]`) |\n| 502 | FHIR server failure; if `patientId` is returned, retry with the same `screeningId` |\n\nEnumerations: `outcome` = cleared | referred | suspected; `pointOfEntry.type` = airport | seaport | border | facility | community; `travelHistory.travelled` = yes | no | unknown; `travelHistory.trips[].means` = land | air | water; countries = ISO 3166 alpha-2 codes from **Lookups > List countries** (e.g. `UG`, `CD`, `KE`); symptom `code` = fever, cough, sore-throat, difficulty-breathing, headache, fatigue, muscle-pain, vomiting, diarrhoea, abdominal-pain, rash, bleeding, jaundice, confusion, other; identifier `type` = Temporary ID, Alien ID, Refugee ID, Mandate Number, Birth Certificate, National ID, Birth Notification, ClientRegistry ID. Dates are `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\nIn query strings, encode `|` as `%7C` (e.g. `_tag=<system>%7C<code>`); the FHIR server rejects a raw `|` with 400.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/provider/login",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "provider",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Log in with the screening service account. Saves `access_token` to `{{token}}` and `refresh_token` to `{{refresh_token}}`.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"idNumber\": \"{{serviceIdNumber}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{servicePassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const t = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token\", t.access_token);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refresh_token\", t.refresh_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Token",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refresh_token\": \"{{refresh_token}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/provider/refresh_token",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "provider",
                "refresh_token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exchange `{{refresh_token}}` for a new token pair."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const t = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token\", t.access_token);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refresh_token\", t.refresh_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Lookups",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List countries",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/provider/screenings/countries",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "provider",
                "screenings",
                "countries"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The 197 countries the vhf-case form offers for travel origin and destination (system `urn:iso:std:iso:3166`). Send the 2-letter `code` in `travelHistory.trips[].country` and `travelHistory.destination.country`; the `display` is stored with it. Country names are also accepted and mapped to the code."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"lists 197 countries\", () => pm.expect(body.countries).to.have.lengthOf(197));",
                  "pm.test(\"includes Uganda as UG\", () => pm.expect(body.countries).to.deep.include({ code: \"UG\", display: \"Uganda\" }));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Submit Screening",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Submit screening - full",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/provider/screenings",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "provider",
                "screenings"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Full payload: point of entry, demographics, travel history and symptoms. Generates a new `screeningId` and saves the returned `patientId` / `questionnaireResponseId`.\n\n`travelHistory` fills the vhf-case Travel History section: `travelled` (yes|no|unknown, or boolean `hasTravelled`), `trips[]` { `country` (ISO code), `city`, `departureDate`, `means` (land|air|water), `arrivalDate`, `purpose` }, `stopovers`, `destination` { `country` (ISO code, default KE), `place` (default point of entry) }. Dates cannot be in the future and arrival cannot be before departure. Get the country codes from **Lookups > List countries**.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"screeningId\": \"{{screeningId}}\",\n  \"screenedAt\": \"{{screenedAt}}\",\n  \"outcome\": \"referred\",\n  \"pointOfEntry\": {\n    \"name\": \"JKIA\",\n    \"type\": \"airport\"\n  },\n  \"patient\": {\n    \"identifiers\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"National ID\",\n        \"value\": \"{{patientIdNumber}}\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"givenNames\": [\n      \"Jane\",\n      \"Wanjiru\"\n    ],\n    \"familyName\": \"Doe\",\n    \"gender\": \"female\",\n    \"birthDate\": \"1990-05-14\",\n    \"phone\": \"0712345678\",\n    \"nationality\": \"KE\",\n    \"address\": {\n      \"county\": \"Nairobi\",\n      \"subCounty\": \"Embakasi East\",\n      \"ward\": \"Utawala\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"travelHistory\": {\n    \"travelled\": \"yes\",\n    \"trips\": [\n      {\n        \"country\": \"UG\",\n        \"city\": \"Kampala\",\n        \"departureDate\": \"2026-10-01\",\n        \"means\": \"air\",\n        \"arrivalDate\": \"2026-10-12\",\n        \"purpose\": \"Business\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"stopovers\": \"None\",\n    \"destination\": {\n      \"country\": \"KE\",\n      \"place\": \"Nairobi\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"signsAndSymptoms\": {\n    \"temperatureCelsius\": 38.4,\n    \"symptoms\": [\n      {\n        \"code\": \"fever\",\n        \"present\": true,\n        \"onsetDate\": \"2026-10-11\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"code\": \"headache\",\n        \"present\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"code\": \"bleeding\",\n        \"present\": false\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Fresh screeningId per run; Retry reuses it to show idempotency",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"screeningId\", pm.variables.replaceIn(\"{{$guid}}\"));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"screenedAt\", new Date().toISOString());",
                  "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get(\"patientIdNumber\")) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"patientIdNumber\", String(Math.floor(10000000 + Math.random() * 89999999)));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"201 Created or 200 matched\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"not a duplicate\", () => pm.expect(b.duplicate).to.eql(false));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"patientId\", b.patientId);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"questionnaireResponseId\", b.questionnaireResponseId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Retry same screeningId (idempotent)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/provider/screenings",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "provider",
                "screenings"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Resends the previous request's `screeningId`; expect `200` with `duplicate: true` and the same ids.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"screeningId\": \"{{screeningId}}\",\n  \"screenedAt\": \"{{screenedAt}}\",\n  \"outcome\": \"referred\",\n  \"pointOfEntry\": {\n    \"name\": \"JKIA\",\n    \"type\": \"airport\"\n  },\n  \"patient\": {\n    \"identifiers\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"National ID\",\n        \"value\": \"{{patientIdNumber}}\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"givenNames\": [\n      \"Jane\",\n      \"Wanjiru\"\n    ],\n    \"familyName\": \"Doe\",\n    \"gender\": \"female\",\n    \"birthDate\": \"1990-05-14\",\n    \"phone\": \"0712345678\",\n    \"nationality\": \"KE\",\n    \"address\": {\n      \"county\": \"Nairobi\",\n      \"subCounty\": \"Embakasi East\",\n      \"ward\": \"Utawala\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"travelHistory\": {\n    \"travelled\": \"yes\",\n    \"trips\": [\n      {\n        \"country\": \"UG\",\n        \"city\": \"Kampala\",\n        \"departureDate\": \"2026-10-01\",\n        \"means\": \"air\",\n        \"arrivalDate\": \"2026-10-12\",\n        \"purpose\": \"Business\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"stopovers\": \"None\",\n    \"destination\": {\n      \"country\": \"KE\",\n      \"place\": \"Nairobi\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"signsAndSymptoms\": {\n    \"temperatureCelsius\": 38.4,\n    \"symptoms\": [\n      {\n        \"code\": \"fever\",\n        \"present\": true,\n        \"onsetDate\": \"2026-10-11\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"code\": \"headache\",\n        \"present\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"code\": \"bleeding\",\n        \"present\": false\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"duplicate\", () => pm.expect(b.duplicate).to.eql(true));",
                  "pm.test(\"same patient\", () => pm.expect(b.patientId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"patientId\")));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Re-screen same person (matches patient)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/provider/screenings",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "provider",
                "screenings"
              ]
            },
            "description": "New `screeningId`, same identifier: matches the existing patient (`200`, `patientCreated: false`) and adds a second screening.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"screeningId\": \"{{screeningId}}\",\n  \"outcome\": \"cleared\",\n  \"patient\": {\n    \"identifiers\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"National ID\",\n        \"value\": \"{{patientIdNumber}}\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"travelHistory\": {\n    \"hasTravelled\": false\n  },\n  \"signsAndSymptoms\": {\n    \"temperatureCelsius\": 36.7\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"screeningId\", pm.variables.replaceIn(\"{{$guid}}\"));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 matched\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"existing patient\", () => {",
                  "    const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(b.patientCreated).to.eql(false);",
                  "    pm.expect(b.patientId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"patientId\"));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Submit screening - minimal",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/provider/screenings",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "provider",
                "screenings"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Smallest valid body.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"screeningId\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n  \"patient\": {\n    \"identifiers\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"National ID\",\n        \"value\": \"{{patientIdNumber}}\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 or 201\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Invalid payload (400)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/provider/screenings",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "provider",
                "screenings"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every problem is reported in `errors[]`, including unknown countries, an unknown `means`, and an arrival before departure.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"screeningId\": \"\",\n  \"outcome\": \"unknown\",\n  \"patient\": {\n    \"identifiers\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Passport\",\n        \"value\": \"X1\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"birthDate\": \"14/05/1990\"\n  },\n  \"signsAndSymptoms\": {\n    \"symptoms\": [\n      {\n        \"code\": \"sneezing\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"travelHistory\": {\n    \"travelled\": \"yes\",\n    \"trips\": [\n      {\n        \"country\": \"Atlantis\",\n        \"departureDate\": \"2026-10-12\",\n        \"arrivalDate\": \"2026-10-01\",\n        \"means\": \"rail\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"400 Bad Request\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test(\"lists errors\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().errors).to.be.an(\"array\").that.is.not.empty);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Find Screenings",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List screened patients",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/provider/screenings/patients?_count=50&_sort=-_lastUpdated",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "provider",
                "screenings",
                "patients"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "_count",
                  "value": "50",
                  "description": "Page size, max 200"
                },
                {
                  "key": "_sort",
                  "value": "-_lastUpdated"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "FHIR Bundle of patients tagged `record-origin|screened`. Optional: `name`, `identifier`, `_count` (max 200), `_offset`, `_sort`."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"is a Bundle\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().resourceType).to.eql(\"Bundle\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Find screened patient by identifier",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/provider/screenings/patients?identifier={{patientIdNumber}}",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "provider",
                "screenings",
                "patients"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "identifier",
                  "value": "{{patientIdNumber}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Look up the patient created above by its identifier number."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get screened Patient (FHIR)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/fhir/Patient/{{patientId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "fhir",
                "Patient",
                "{{patientId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The patient via the FHIR proxy."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"is the screened patient\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"patientId\")));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Screenings for patient (FHIR)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/fhir/QuestionnaireResponse?subject=Patient/{{patientId}}&_profile=http://nphiis.health.go.ke/fhir/StructureDefinition/traveller-screening-response",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "fhir",
                "QuestionnaireResponse"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "subject",
                  "value": "Patient/{{patientId}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "_profile",
                  "value": "http://nphiis.health.go.ke/fhir/StructureDefinition/traveller-screening-response"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "All screenings recorded for `{{patientId}}`."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"has the patient's screenings\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().entry || []).to.have.length.of.at.least(2));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Screenings by outcome (FHIR)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API_HOST}}/fhir/QuestionnaireResponse?_tag=http://nphiis.health.go.ke/fhir/CodeSystem/screening-outcome%7Creferred",
              "host": [
                "{{API_HOST}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "fhir",
                "QuestionnaireResponse"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "_tag",
                  "value": "http://nphiis.health.go.ke/fhir/CodeSystem/screening-outcome%7Creferred"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Filter screenings by outcome tag: cleared | referred | suspected."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
